-- title:
--   Level-q automorphisms fix every Igusa-type valuation ring of K
-- statement:
--   **Data.** Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and let $M'\geq 1$ be a natural number with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((X))$ (`LaurentSeries L`), and assume (`hK`) that $K=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((X))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ ([`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)), of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A\to L$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec} C=$ `XFin` and the corresponding chart for $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and chart inclusion `ιFin`. Throughout, a *level automorphism attached to $\delta\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') δ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero image, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the $\iota$-coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \operatorname{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\delta)$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \operatorname{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\delta)$, where $\operatorname{conjElemN}(m)(\delta)=\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00}&\delta_{01}/m\\ m\delta_{10}&\delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   **The supersingular maximal ideal.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ which is the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin` image $z$ whose prime ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ ([`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)) modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v-fu\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses, which concern: (i) constants, $e$ carrying the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $\sigma a$; (ii) stability, every level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) congruence, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such an automorphism acts as the identity on $C$ modulo $y'$; (iv) equivariance, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and an automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and trivial on $C$ modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ implements $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map, fixes the constants, satisfies $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)S$, with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) branch separation, two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, and containing respective elements $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions to the stalk whenever $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) the Igusa-coefficient clause, for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing the class of $X_0$ plus a term of $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the Hasse-form clause, asserting $\operatorname{jqNModC} L (q\ell)\in K$ and in $C$, an $a_0\in A$ with $\operatorname{jqNModC} L (q\ell)-a_0\in y'$, an $e_0\ge 1$ and an $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ whenever $a,b\in W$ are not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and with $e$ of the germ of $\operatorname{jqNModC} L (q\ell)-a_0$ equal to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The pinned witness.** Data $z$, $\varpi_z$ (with the same two hypotheses), $y'$ over $z$, supersingular (`hss'`) and with $y'$ the prime $y$ (`hy'y`), together with a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, units $u_1,v_1$ and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S_1:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this one witness, exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) just listed.
--
--   **Centre, blow-up algebra and valuation ring.** `hJ` pins the ideal $J$ of $C$ as the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}\bigl(\{a\in C : e_1(\mathrm{germ}_z a)\in(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)S_1\}\bigr)$, taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which map $C$ into $C$. `hB` pins the $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ as the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K: x\varpi_t\in J\}$, that is $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and four hypothesis blocks are imposed: `hR1` (two clauses) that $C\subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2` (three clauses) that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) that $W\cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the complement of $\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k_A[X_0,X_1]$ by $(\operatorname{drinfeldPoly} q\,k_A-1)$) with kernel $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to k_A$, and, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, equivariant for an element $c\in\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\operatorname{redQ} q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) — the kernel of $(\bar\gamma,c)\mapsto\det(\bar\gamma)c^{q+1}$ — acting through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c\neq 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to inverses of elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached, in the sense stated there, by some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ carrying $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$ into it; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates by level automorphisms attached to inverses of elements of $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, which preserves $y$ on $C$ also preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that
--
--   1. an element of $L$ lies in $V$ if and only if it comes from $A$;
--
--   2. the image of $\varpi$ lies in $V$ and in $\mathfrak m_V$;
--
--   3. every element of $C$ lies in $V$; and
--
--   4. there is $c\in C$ such that for every monic polynomial $p\in A[T]$ the value $p(c)$ (formed in $K$ via $A\to K$) lies in $V$ and is a unit of $V$;
--
--   and for every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ that is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$: for all $f\in K$ one has $f\in V$ if and only if $\tau f\in V$.
--
--   The conclusion is about an arbitrary $V$ subject to (1)–(4); the pinned ring $W$ and the algebras $J$, $B$ enter only as hypotheses.
--
--   Condition (4) says that the reduction of some element of the $j$-finite chart algebra is transcendental over the residue field of $A$, so the valuation rings $V$ in the conclusion are exactly those cutting out a component of the special fibre of the integral model that dominates the supersingular chart in the manner of Igusa's analysis; the statement asserts that the level-$q$ part of the level structure acts trivially on the set of such components. It is the load-bearing input for the stability of the end neighbourhoods in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), and is also used for the separation of translates and for the comparison of supersingular primes in the two further assemblies that cite it.
